WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.422
Imagine four boxes with six pencils each. Seven
pencils are given away. How many are left?

00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:08.592
A language model could guess a number immediately.
What changes

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:11.373
if we give it room to work through the problem?

00:00:11.763 --> 00:00:13.912
Earlier chain-of-thought prompting showed the model

00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:16.419
worked examples before asking a new question.

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:21.035
Kojima and colleagues tried a shorter prompt that
needs no demonstrations.

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:26.812
Keep the question and add one sentence at the start
of the answer: Let's think step by step.

00:00:27.202 --> 00:00:30.406
The first model call continues that sentence. In this

00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:33.610
example, it multiplies four by six to get
twenty-four.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.769
Then it subtracts seven to get seventeen. That

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.538
whole continuation becomes part of the second prompt.

00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:43.002
The second call sees the original prompt, the
generated

00:00:43.002 --> 00:00:46.418
working, and a cue asking for the answer in numerals.

00:00:46.808 --> 00:00:49.467
The experiment then parses the completion into a

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:52.126
scoreable answer. Both calls use the same model.

00:00:52.516 --> 00:00:56.103
On MultiArith, text davinci zero zero two scored

00:00:56.103 --> 00:00:59.690
seventeen point seven percent with direct zero-shot
prompting.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.325
Let's think step by step raised it to seventy-eight

00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:06.930
point seven. Let's think by itself scored fifty-seven
point five.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.403
Even First, followed by a comma, reached

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.926
seventy-seven point three. Abrakadabra scored fifteen
point five.

00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:18.902
Wording mattered in this experiment, and several
different cues could start useful working.

00:01:19.292 --> 00:01:22.122
On GSM eight K, the eight-billion-parameter PaLM went

00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:25.306
from two point one to two point four percent.

00:01:25.696 --> 00:01:30.294
The five-hundred-forty-billion-parameter model went
from twelve point five to forty-three.

00:01:30.684 --> 00:01:34.332
For that larger model, sampling forty reasoning paths
and voting on

00:01:34.332 --> 00:01:38.312
their final answers pushed GSM eight K accuracy to
seventy point one.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.842
The gains varied by task. On Commonsense Q A,

00:01:41.842 --> 00:01:44.982
text davinci scored lower with the extra reasoning
prompt.

00:01:45.372 --> 00:01:48.115
A short instruction can make a capable model

00:01:48.115 --> 00:01:51.201
write useful intermediate steps before committing to
an answer.

00:01:51.591 --> 00:01:54.371
Check the final answer on the task you care

00:01:54.371 --> 00:01:57.152
about. A clear-looking explanation can still contain
a mistake.
